---
/**
 * The employment application, on `/careers/`.
 *
 * **Why not `EnquiryForm`.** That one asks an events question — headcount and a
 * date — because a planner arrives knowing both. Someone looking for work knows
 * neither, and being asked "how many people" is the form telling them they are
 * on the wrong page. The plumbing is shared (`/api/lead`, the honeypot, the
 * signed stamp, `LeadFormScript`); the field set is not. Same split as
 * `LessonEnquiryForm`.
 *
 * **`role` is the load-bearing field, and it is free text on purpose.** There
 * are no named openings, so a select would mean inventing three or four job
 * titles and quietly asserting that those are the jobs that exist here. Nobody
 * has said they do. Asking in the applicant's own words costs a tidy spreadsheet
 * column and buys an answer that is actually true — and it is the one line that
 * decides whether there is a conversation to have, so it goes first, above the
 * rule, the way `lessonFor` does on the lessons form.
 *
 * ── WHAT THIS FORM DELIBERATELY DOES NOT ASK ────────────────────────────────
 *
 * No date of birth. No work-eligibility attestation. No background-history
 * question. No EEO monitoring fields. Every one of those is a legal instrument
 * rather than a form field: it needs an employer decision and a lawyer behind
 * it, several of them are regulated as to WHEN in the process they may be asked
 * at all, and every answer would land in a spreadsheet that more than one person
 * can open. They belong wherever the venue handles an actual offer. Do not add
 * one here because a template elsewhere had it.
 *
 * **No resume upload.** The lead pipeline is a sheet row plus a notification and
 * has no file store; building one is a real piece of work and not a field. So
 * the page asks for a resume by email to the same address the notification goes
 * to (`hr@lakevillelinks.com`, the `employment` list's `notify`), which means
 * the two halves of an application meet in one inbox rather than in two systems.
 * If a file store is ever added, this is the note to come back to.
 *
 * **It does not ask which venue, and that is a fact rather than an omission.**
 * The Links employs nobody at Stillwater (owner, 2026-09-14), so every other
 * form on this site opens with a venue question and this one must not: offering
 * a choice of two would invite applications for jobs that do not exist, and
 * offering a select with one option in it is a question with no question in it.
 * The venue is passed in and recorded on the row instead, so the spreadsheet
 * column stays populated and the day Stillwater does hire, this becomes a real
 * field again rather than a hidden value nobody remembers is there.
 *
 * A greige slab on the page's white ground, matching `LessonEnquiryForm` — the
 * same component doing the same job, so it should not look like a new thing.
 *
 * Posts to `/api/lead/` — fixed and same-origin, like every other form here.
 * Works with JavaScript disabled: a native POST gets a 303 to `/thanks/`, and
 * `LeadFormScript` upgrades that to an inline confirmation.
 *
 * ⚠️ **Keep the trailing slash on that action.** `trailingSlash: 'always'`
 * applies to API routes as well as pages: under `astro dev`, `POST /api/lead`
 * is a 404 and `POST /api/lead/` works. Production 308s the slashless form, so
 * dropping the slash breaks local testing ONLY — and silently. It must also stay
 * identical to `ENDPOINT` in `LeadFormScript.astro`, which selects forms by
 * `action`. See FW-4023.
 */
import { buttonClasses } from '../../lib/buttons';

interface Props {
  heading?: string;
  blurb?: string;
  listName: string;
  /**
   * The venue slug recorded on the row. NOT asked of the applicant — see the
   * header. Passed in so the one place that knows which venues hire is the page,
   * not this component.
   */
  venue: string;
  /** Where a resume should be sent. Rendered in the copy AND in the success message. */
  hrEmail: string;
  id?: string;
  class?: string;
}

const {
  heading = 'Apply to work here',
  blurb = 'There is no closing date and nothing to upload. Tell us what you are after and when you can work, and someone will read it. If you have a resume, send it along separately — the address is under the form.',
  listName,
  venue,
  hrEmail,
  id,
  class: className = '',
} = Astro.props;

const formId = id ?? `job-application-${listName.replace(/\W+/g, '-').toLowerCase()}`;

const field =
  'min-h-tap w-full min-w-0 rounded-control border-rule border-navy bg-white px-s4 py-s3 text-body text-navy placeholder:text-inkMuted';
const labelClass = 'caps-label block text-label-sm text-inkMuted';
---

<div class:list={['bg-greige border-t-score border-primary p-cell lg:p-cell-lg', className]}>
  <h2 class="text-section leading-display font-extrabold tracking-display-tight text-ink">{heading}</h2>
  <p class="mt-s3 max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-inkBody">{blurb}</p>

  <form
    class="mt-s6"
    action="/api/lead/"
    method="POST"
    data-analytics={`application:${listName}`}
    data-success="Thanks — we have got it, and someone will read it. If you are sending a resume, hr@lakevillelinks.com is the address."
    id={formId}
  >
    <input type="hidden" name="list" value={listName} />
    {/* Recorded, not asked. See the header. */}
    <input type="hidden" name="venue" value={venue} />
    <input type="hidden" name="_page" value={Astro.url.pathname} />
    {/* Filled at runtime by LeadFormScript; absent on the no-JS path, which is accepted. */}
    <input type="hidden" name="_ts" value="" />
    <input type="text" name="_hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" class="hidden" aria-hidden="true" />

    {
      /* The question the rest of it turns on, first and alone above the 4px
        rule — the same move the lessons form makes with who the lesson is for.
        A text input rather than a menu: see the header. The placeholder gives
        two examples so the field is not intimidating, and neither of them
        claims a vacancy. */
    }
    <div class="border-b-score border-navy pb-s6">
      <label class={labelClass} for={`${formId}-role`}>What kind of work you are looking for</label>
      <input
        id={`${formId}-role`}
        name="role"
        type="text"
        required
        placeholder='In your own words — "behind the bar" and "anything going" are both fine answers.'
        class={`mt-s2 ${field}`}
      />
    </div>

    {
      /* Five cells, every slot filled: name and email pair, then phone pairs
        with availability rather than leaving a hole beside it. The venue select
        that used to lead this grid is gone — see the header. */
    }
    <div class="mt-s6 grid gap-s5 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <label class={labelClass} for={`${formId}-name`}>Your name</label>
        <input id={`${formId}-name`} name="name" type="text" required class={`mt-s2 ${field}`} />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label class={labelClass} for={`${formId}-email`}>Email</label>
        <input id={`${formId}-email`} name="email" type="email" required class={`mt-s2 ${field}`} />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label class={labelClass} for={`${formId}-phone`}>Phone</label>
        <input id={`${formId}-phone`} name="phone" type="tel" class={`mt-s2 ${field}`} />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label class={labelClass} for={`${formId}-availability`}>When you can work</label>
        <input
          id={`${formId}-availability`}
          name="availability"
          type="text"
          placeholder="Evenings, weekends, weekday daytimes."
          class={`mt-s2 ${field}`}
        />
      </div>
      <div class="sm:col-span-2">
        <label class={labelClass} for={`${formId}-message`}>Anything you want us to know</label>
        <textarea
          id={`${formId}-message`}
          name="message"
          rows="5"
          placeholder="Where you have worked before, if anywhere. It is genuinely fine if this is your first job."
          class={`mt-s2 ${field}`}></textarea>
      </div>
    </div>

    <button type="submit" class:list={[buttonClasses('md', 'primary'), 'mt-s6 w-full cursor-pointer']}>
      Send my application
    </button>

    <p class="mt-s4 max-w-prose-page text-small leading-body text-inkBody">
      Got a resume? Email it to <a href={`mailto:${hrEmail}`} class="font-semibold underline">{hrEmail}</a> — it reaches the
      same person this form does. You do not need one to apply.
    </p>

    {/* Only ever shown on failure — success replaces the whole form. */}
    <p
      data-lead-status
      role="alert"
      hidden
      class="mt-s4 border-l-slab border-accent pl-s4 text-small leading-body text-inkBody"
    >
    </p>
  </form>
</div>
